The five-archetype idea (Prototyper, Builder, Sweeper, Grower, Maintainer) comes from
Boris Cherny (creator of Claude Code), public post on X, June 2026.

The archetype structure and the four templates in templates/ are adapted from
https://github.com/mfreidlitz/claude-agent-archetypes (commit 514bf57), MIT License,
Copyright (c) 2026 Michael Freidlitz.

The product-stage mix (new = prototyper+builder+sweeper, growing = builder+sweeper+grower and
some maintainer, mature = sweeper+grower+maintainer and some builder) is taken from the same post
by Boris Cherny.

The mechanical gates (scripts/gate.py, scripts/guard_hook.py), the attempt ledger
(scripts/attempts.py) and the stepped maintainer levels (L1 report, L2 assisted, L3 unattended)
follow ideas from https://github.com/cobusgreyling/loop-engineering (loop-gate, loop-context,
readiness levels), MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 Cobus Greyling and contributors. No code was
copied; the scripts here were written for this package.

Thanks to Flowstate Technologies, whose build protocol ("DEF" / The Loop: align, research with
sources, plan in pieces with re-runnable proofs, lock in, run with proofs re-run) is the host
protocol this package was designed to graft onto, and against which it was tested. That host
protocol is a separate, closed-source work of Flowstate Technologies; this package does not include
any of its text and does not require it to be installed somewhere else first — the hooks in
skills/def-infinity/SKILL.md describe where they attach in plain terms, so the graft can be adapted
to any similarly-shaped plan-first protocol.

This package contains only the graft. It does not include the text of the host build
protocol it was designed for.
